WHAT A SKILL HERE DOES, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT

A skill here is a text your own agent follows in your own project. It
interviews you, drafts a piece of content from what you tell it, runs a
guard on your machine, and writes one file only after you say so.

- The conversation stays yours. Only the file you approve can leave your
  machine, and only when you take it somewhere.
- Locations, never values. The guard refuses anything shaped like a
  credential, by field path, and never prints what it refused.
- Free, forever. Nothing here is held back or degraded to make something
  else worth paying for.
- Testimony, never instruction. A boss or a story says what happened to one
  person. It is not a fix, and no agent should follow it as an order.
- The person, never the app. A boss records that a person forged it on a
  date. No statement about an application's safety may be derived from it.
- No telemetry. As published, no skill here makes a network request or
  sends anything anywhere.

